    "details": "<p><strong>Hackers Gambit 2026 &ndash; International Capture The Flag (CTF) Competition</strong></p>\n<p>Hackers Gambit 2026 is an <strong data-start=\"323\" data-end=\"381\">International-Level Capture The Flag (CTF) Competition</strong> organized by <strong data-start=\"395\" data-end=\"419\">JCOE Cyber Sentinels</strong>, Jaihind College of Engineering, Kuran. The event aims to bring together students, cybersecurity enthusiasts, researchers, and professionals from around the world to compete in a challenging cybersecurity competition designed to test technical expertise, analytical thinking, and problem-solving skills.</p>\n<p>The competition consists of <strong data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"767\">two stages</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &ndash;</strong> Online Qualifier (48 Hours)</p>\n<ul data-start=\"816\" data-end=\"960\">\n<li data-section-id=\"i8lek3\" data-start=\"816\" data-end=\"859\"><strong data-start=\"818\" data-end=\"827\">Date:</strong> 2 October 2026 &ndash; 4 October 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1b24lju\" data-start=\"860\" data-end=\"916\"><strong data-start=\"862\" data-end=\"871\">Time:</strong> 12:00 PM IST (2 Oct) to 12:00 PM IST (4 Oct)</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"197ezjy\" data-start=\"917\" data-end=\"935\"><strong data-start=\"919\" data-end=\"928\">Mode:</strong> Online</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"vdtnxv\" data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"960\"><strong data-start=\"938\" data-end=\"951\">Duration:</strong> 48 Hours</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Participants will solve real-world cybersecurity challenges across multiple categories, including:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1062\" data-end=\"1239\">\n<li data-section-id=\"7k8cy6\" data-start=\"1062\" data-end=\"1076\">Web Security</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"3j9oda\" data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1091\">Cryptography</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"psxvox\" data-start=\"1092\" data-end=\"1113\">Reverse Engineering</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"pgibag\" data-start=\"1114\" data-end=\"1133\">Digital Forensics</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"nawwtd\" data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1161\">Binary Exploitation (Pwn)</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1gnlkmy\" data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1196\">Open Source Intelligence (OSINT)</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"2v33iw\" data-start=\"1197\" data-end=\"1212\">Steganography</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"14qv33e\" data-start=\"1213\" data-end=\"1239\">Miscellaneous Challenges</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The online qualifier will determine the <strong data-start=\"1281\" data-end=\"1297\">Top 15 teams</strong>, who will advance to the Grand Finale.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &ndash;</strong> Grand Finale (Offline)</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1384\" data-end=\"1604\">\n<li data-section-id=\"av1ohg\" data-start=\"1384\" data-end=\"1429\"><strong data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1395\">Date:</strong> 30 October 2026 &ndash; 31 October 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"dcxwnx\" data-start=\"1430\" data-end=\"1488\"><strong data-start=\"1432\" data-end=\"1441\">Time:</strong> 12:00 PM IST (30 Oct) to 12:00 PM IST (31 Oct)</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"5a7mz4\" data-start=\"1489\" data-end=\"1508\"><strong data-start=\"1491\" data-end=\"1500\">Mode:</strong> Offline</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"knhin7\" data-start=\"1509\" data-end=\"1579\"><strong data-start=\"1511\" data-end=\"1521\">Venue:</strong> Jaihind College of Engineering, Kuran, Maharashtra, India</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"f4itdl\" data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1604\"><strong data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1595\">Duration:</strong> 24 Hours</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The finalists will compete in an intensive 24-hour CTF featuring advanced security challenges designed to test technical depth, teamwork, endurance, and creativity.</p>\n<p>The competition concludes with the Prize Distribution and Closing Ceremony.</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1869\" data-end=\"2265\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1qkojj0\" data-start=\"1869\" data-end=\"1915\">Open to participants from <strong data-start=\"1897\" data-end=\"1914\">all countries</strong>.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1wtlt8m\" data-start=\"1916\" data-end=\"1998\">Students, researchers, professionals, and cybersecurity enthusiasts are welcome.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1c9z5yh\" data-start=\"1999\" data-end=\"2084\">Participants must comply with all competition rules and ethical hacking guidelines.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1gbmxla\" data-start=\"2085\" data-end=\"2146\">No prior professional cybersecurity experience is required.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1qswggs\" data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2265\">Participants below 18 years of age should obtain parental or institutional consent if required by local regulations.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Team Formation:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2290\" data-end=\"2678\">\n<li data-section-id=\"lk1etw\" data-start=\"2290\" data-end=\"2328\">Individual participation is allowed.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"187wlsw\" data-start=\"2329\" data-end=\"2361\">Team participation is allowed.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"juphz7\" data-start=\"2362\" data-end=\"2395\">Maximum 3 members per team.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"16cjfyc\" data-start=\"2396\" data-end=\"2434\">Inter-college teams are allowed.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"pwjxgr\" data-start=\"2435\" data-end=\"2476\">Inter-university teams are allowed.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"13096rk\" data-start=\"2477\" data-end=\"2522\">Inter-specialization teams are allowed.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"51cyd8\" data-start=\"2523\" data-end=\"2561\"><strong data-start=\"2525\" data-end=\"2561\">International teams are allowed.</strong></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1k8c732\" data-start=\"2562\" data-end=\"2678\">Team composition cannot be changed after registrations close without prior approval from the organizing committee.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Format</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Online Qualifier:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2729\" data-end=\"2991\">\n<li data-section-id=\"pm2kx2\" data-start=\"2729\" data-end=\"2775\">Jeopardy-style Capture The Flag competition.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"w51yq0\" data-start=\"2776\" data-end=\"2829\">Multiple categories with varying difficulty levels.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1ricpx8\" data-start=\"2830\" data-end=\"2872\">Challenges carry different point values.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"14cmibm\" data-start=\"2873\" data-end=\"2910\">Dynamic scoring may be implemented.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"lr8rs9\" data-start=\"2911\" data-end=\"2991\">Live leaderboard throughout the competition (subject to organizer discretion).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Grand Finale:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"3011\" data-end=\"3252\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1q2y8sl\" data-start=\"3011\" data-end=\"3064\">Advanced Jeopardy-style CTF with higher difficulty.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1q6i2fi\" data-start=\"3065\" data-end=\"3126\">Additional real-world security scenarios may be introduced.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"17p9w32\" data-start=\"3127\" data-end=\"3179\">Teams compete on-site under supervised conditions.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"fsqz38\" data-start=\"3180\" data-end=\"3252\">Final rankings are determined based on score and challenge completion.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Write-up Submission:</strong></p>\n<p>Following the online qualifier, participants may be required to submit technical write-ups explaining their solutions for selected challenges.</p>\n<p>Write-ups will be evaluated for:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"3460\" data-end=\"3540\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1tn5esm\" data-start=\"3460\" data-end=\"3480\">Technical accuracy</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"cnexw5\" data-start=\"3481\" data-end=\"3494\">Originality</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1nd1o9b\" data-start=\"3495\" data-end=\"3515\">Proper methodology</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1eedr61\" data-start=\"3516\" data-end=\"3540\">Fair play verification</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Failure to submit the required write-up within the deadline may affect qualification for the Grand Finale.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"3664\" data-end=\"4470\">\n<li data-section-id=\"tcuvql\" data-start=\"3664\" data-end=\"3724\">Participants must use only their own skills and knowledge.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"157my7p\" data-start=\"3725\" data-end=\"3820\">Sharing flags, solutions, or challenge content during the competition is strictly prohibited.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"wacrsz\" data-start=\"3821\" data-end=\"3916\">Attacking the competition infrastructure or other participant systems is strictly prohibited.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1t4a39l\" data-start=\"3917\" data-end=\"3974\">Denial-of-Service (DoS/DDoS) attacks are not permitted.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"rugwz8\" data-start=\"3975\" data-end=\"4106\">Any attempt to compromise the CTF platform, organizers' infrastructure, or other teams will result in immediate disqualification.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"a491d2\" data-start=\"4107\" data-end=\"4201\">Automated exploitation tools are allowed only where explicitly permitted by challenge rules.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"o0nsn2\" data-start=\"4202\" data-end=\"4305\">Organizers reserve the right to request write-ups or additional verification for challenge solutions.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1nk76j6\" data-start=\"4306\" data-end=\"4404\">Any form of plagiarism, impersonation, collusion, or unfair means will lead to disqualification.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1fnrnj7\" data-start=\"4405\" data-end=\"4470\">The organizing committee's decision shall be final and binding.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria:</strong></p>\n<p>Teams will be evaluated based on:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"4532\" data-end=\"4701\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1w46kks\" data-start=\"4532\" data-end=\"4553\">Total points earned</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1oqg30c\" data-start=\"4554\" data-end=\"4596\">Number of successfully solved challenges</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"m2deld\" data-start=\"4597\" data-end=\"4623\">Correct flag submissions</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"8ej1v4\" data-start=\"4624\" data-end=\"4665\">Quality of required technical write-ups</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"uppg73\" data-start=\"4666\" data-end=\"4701\">Compliance with competition rules</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important Dates:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"4727\" data-end=\"5042\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1978i0b\" data-start=\"4766\" data-end=\"4810\"><strong data-start=\"4768\" data-end=\"4792\">Registration Closes:</strong> 26 September 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"69tjec\" data-start=\"4811\" data-end=\"4851\"><strong data-start=\"4813\" data-end=\"4834\">Online Qualifier:</strong> 2&ndash;4 October 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"jbqn6i\" data-start=\"4852\" data-end=\"4895\"><strong data-start=\"4854\" data-end=\"4878\">Write-up Submission:</strong> 4&ndash;6 October 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1c6itzr\" data-start=\"4896\" data-end=\"4944\"><strong data-start=\"4898\" data-end=\"4928\">Top 15 Teams Announcement:</strong> 10 October 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1al4lv7\" data-start=\"4945\" data-end=\"4993\"><strong data-start=\"4947\" data-end=\"4974\">Grand Finale (Offline):</strong> 30&ndash;31 October 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1c6ow9j\" data-start=\"4994\" data-end=\"5042\"><strong data-start=\"4996\" data-end=\"5026\">Awards &amp; Closing Ceremony:</strong> 31 October 2026</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"5059\" data-end=\"5330\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1k18vzm\" data-start=\"5059\" data-end=\"5160\">Cash prizes, trophies, certificates, sponsor goodies, and exclusive rewards will be announced soon.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1xmp415\" data-start=\"5161\" data-end=\"5242\">Every verified participant will receive a digital Certificate of Participation.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"fqzrdf\" data-start=\"5243\" data-end=\"5330\">Winners and finalists will receive certificates of achievement and other recognition.</li>\n</ul>",
